## 1. Offline preloader now uses the same fallback — [index.html](index.html), [sw.js](sw.js)

The preloader used to do `cacheIframe.src = g.url` — the raw `gamebackup.github.io` URL. On a filtered network that loads the block page, so it "succeeded" at caching a block page. Now:

- **One shared resolution path.** I extracted `x3eResolveCandidates(cands)` out of `x3eLaunchViaMirrors`, so `playGame` and the preloader both use the exact same parallel race. If no host answers, the picker marks that game ⚠️ and moves on instead of pretending it cached.
- **It remembers *where* each game came from.** New `x3e-cachedBases` map. This was necessary: files cached under a mirror obviously don't start with the game's own URL, so the old `cached.startsWith(gameUrl)` check in `openGamePicker`/`handleCachedUrlsResponse` would have **silently dropped every mirror-preloaded game** on the next visit. That logic is now `cachedPrefixesFor()`, and `purgeAllGameCaches` clears both locations.
- **The service worker had to change too**, or the feature would be half-useless: it can now serve back cached mirror responses in normal mode (`X3E_MIRROR_HOSTS`, read-only — it never writes mirror traffic to the cache), and `CLEAR_GAME` accepts mirror-host prefixes. Before, purging a mirror-cached game would have been silently refused by the old `gamebackup.github.io`-only safety guard.

## 2. Guide is current — [successor-guide.md](successor-guide.md)

- `x3e-offline-v2` → **`x3e-offline-v3`** (both places it appeared).
- New **"### Mirror Failover"** section: the parallel race, the budgets, why `<base>` injection is needed, the dead-host memory, and the "add a mirror here *and* in sw.js" rule.
- New **"### The Game Proxy (`proxy/`)"** section, including the blunt hostname caveat and the note that `finalproduct-v2.html` never needs touching.
- Updated §2 and §3 (proxy dir, new feature bullets, corrected SW modes), a §9 troubleshooting bullet for "every game is blocked", a §10 checklist item, and §11's constants table rebuilt — every line number in it verified against the actual files.

## Verification

- All 6 inline `<script>` blocks in `index.html` parse — 0 errors. `node --check sw.js` clean. Proxy smoke test still 6/6.
- I wrote a throwaway harness that loaded the **real preloader script block** with a DOM stub and ran 6 assertions against the actual code. It caught a genuine bug I'd otherwise have shipped: a stale `cachedBases` record could *hide* a file that really was cached, dropping a valid game. Fixed — `cachedPrefixesFor()` now tests both the recorded origin and the game's own directory — and re-tested. Harness deleted afterward.
- All 15 line numbers I put in the guide's table were re-derived from the files after the last edit, and match.

## What I could not verify

- **Whether a blob-URL document's sub-resource requests are actually intercepted by the service worker.** The mirror-preload path depends on that (blob docs created by a controlled page are controlled — standard behavior), but I didn't measure it, and proving it needs a real browser session with `gamebackup.github.io` deliberately blocked. That's the one step left that only a filtered Chromebook can confirm.
